      "content": "# Universal Template Standard Fields Reference\n\n## Table of Contents\n\n1. [Overview](#overview)\n2. [Identity & Metadata](#identity--metadata)\n3. [Agent Configuration](#agent-configuration)\n4. [Exit Code Processing](#exit-code-processing)\n5. [Output Configuration](#output-configuration)\n6. [Execution Behavior](#execution-behavior)\n7. [Credential Configuration](#credential-configuration)\n8. [Script Configuration](#script-configuration)\n9. [Environment Variables](#environment-variables)\n10. [Logging Configuration](#logging-configuration)\n11. [Field Restrictions](#field-restrictions)\n12. [Runtime Components](#runtime-components)\n13. [Versioning & Import/Export](#versioning--importexport)\n\n---\n\n## Overview\n\nThis document provides a comprehensive reference of all standard template-level properties available in Universal Extension templates. These properties control the extension's identity, execution behavior, agent selection, output handling, and runtime configuration.\n\n**Note:** This document covers template-level properties. For UI field properties (Text, Integer, Boolean, etc.), see **ue-template-standard-extension-fields.md**.\n\n---\n\n## Identity & Metadata\n\nProperties that define the extension's basic identity and descriptive information.\n\n### name\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** Yes\n**Description:** Human-readable display name shown in UAC UI\n**When to Use:** Always required\n**Constraints:** Maximum 99 characters\n**Usual Practice:** Descriptive name that clearly identifies the extension's purpose\n**Example:** `\"Email Notification Extension\"`, `\"SAP Business Technology Platform Application Jobs\"`\n\n---\n\n### extension\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** Yes\n**Description:** Unique system identifier for the extension\n**When to Use:** Always required\n**Constraints:**\n- Use hyphens (not underscores)\n- Must be unique across all templates\n**Example:** `\"kafka-producer\"`, `\"ue-sap-btp-appjobs\"`, `\"email-notification\"`, `random-extension`\n\n---\n\n### description\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Full description of extension purpose and functionality\n**When to Use:** Highly recommended for documentation\n**Constraints:** Maximum 255 characters\n**Usual Practice:** Always provide a clear description; can match the name for simple extensions\n**Example:** `\"Send email notifications via SMTP or MS Graph API with attachment support\"`, `\"SAP Business Technology Platform Application Jobs\"`\n\n---\n\n### sysId\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** Yes\n**Description:** 32-character alphanumeric system identifier\n**When to Use:** NEVER\n**Usual Practice:** Not used, the Controller provides sysId automaticly\n\n---\n\n### templateType\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** Yes\n**Description:** Template classification\n**When to Use:** Always required\n**Valid Values:**\n- `\"Script\"` - Script-based template\n- `\"Extension\"` - Extension framework template (most common)\n**Usual Practice:** Always `\"Extension\"` for Universal Extensions\n**Example:** `\"Extension\"`\n\n---\n\n### variablePrefix\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** Yes\n**Description:** Prefix for auto-generated field variables\n**When to Use:** Always required\n**Constraints:**\n- Maximum 20 characters\n- Lowercase with underscores\n- Should match extension identifier style\n**Format:** `ue_var`\n**Usual Practice:** Always use `ue_var`\n**Example:** `ue_var`\n\n---\n\n## Agent Configuration\n\nProperties that control agent selection and execution targeting.\n\n### agentType\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** Yes\n**Description:** Platform compatibility specification\n**When to Use:** Always required\n**Valid Values:**\n- `\"Any\"` - Platform-agnostic (REST APIs, cross-platform tools)\n- `\"Linux/Unix\"` - Linux/Unix platforms only\n- `\"Windows\"` - Windows platforms only\n- `\"IBM i\"` - IBM i platform only\n**Usual Practice:** Use `\"Any\"` for extensions that work across platforms (most common for API-based extensions)\n**Example:** `\"Any\"`\n\n---\n\n### agent\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Specific agent name for task execution\n**When to Use:** When targeting a specific agent\n**Mutually Exclusive With:** `agentVar`, `broadcastCluster`, `broadcastClusterVar`\n**Usual Practice:** Set to `null` unless specifically targeting a single agent\n**Example:** `\"prod-agent-01\"` or `null`\n\n---\n\n### agentVar\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Variable containing agent name at runtime\n**When to Use:** When agent name is dynamic\n**Mutually Exclusive With:** `agent`, `broadcastCluster`, `broadcastClusterVar`\n**Format:** `\"${VARIABLE_NAME}\"`\n**Usual Practice:** Set to `null` unless using variable-based agent selection\n**Example:** `\"${TARGET_AGENT}\"` or `null`\n\n---\n\n### agentCluster\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Agent cluster name (Controller selects one agent from cluster)\n**When to Use:** Load balancing across multiple agents\n**Mutually Exclusive With:** `agentClusterVar`, `broadcastCluster`, `broadcastClusterVar`\n**Usual Practice:** Set to `null` unless using cluster-based agent selection\n**Example:** `\"production-cluster\"` or `null`\n\n---\n\n### agentClusterVar\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Variable containing agent cluster name at runtime\n**When to Use:** When cluster name is dynamic\n**Mutually Exclusive With:** `agentCluster`, `broadcastCluster`, `broadcastClusterVar`\n**Format:** `\"${VARIABLE_NAME}\"`\n**Usual Practice:** Set to `null` unless using variable-based cluster selection\n**Example:** `\"${TARGET_CLUSTER}\"` or `null`\n\n---\n\n### broadcastCluster\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Cluster for broadcast execution (runs on ALL agents in cluster)\n**When to Use:** When task must execute simultaneously on multiple agents\n**Mutually Exclusive With:** `broadcastClusterVar`, `agent`, `agentVar`, `agentCluster`, `agentClusterVar`\n**Note:** Each agent execution becomes a separate task instance\n**Usual Practice:** Set to `null` unless broadcasting to multiple agents\n**Example:** `\"monitoring-cluster\"` or `null`\n\n---\n\n### broadcastClusterVar\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Variable containing broadcast cluster name at runtime\n**When to Use:** When broadcast cluster name is dynamic\n**Mutually Exclusive With:** `broadcastCluster`, `agent`, `agentVar`, `agentCluster`, `agentClusterVar`\n**Format:** `\"${VARIABLE_NAME}\"`\n**Usual Practice:** Set to `null` unless using variable-based broadcast\n**Example:** `\"${BROADCAST_CLUSTER}\"` or `null`\n\n---\n\n### agentFieldsRestriction\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Visibility restriction for agent selection fields\n**When to Use:** To control agent field visibility in UI\n**Valid Values:**\n- `\"No Restriction\"` (default)\n- `\"Read Only\"`\n- `\"Hidden\"`\n**Usual Practice:** Use `\"No Restriction\"` to allow users to select agents\n**Example:** `\"No Restriction\"`\n\n---\n\n## Exit Code Processing\n\nProperties that control how UAC determines task success or failure.\n\n### exitCodeProcessing\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Strategy for evaluating task success/failure\n**When to Use:** Always specify (defaults to \"Success Exitcode Range\")\n**Valid Values:**\n- `\"Success Exitcode Range\"` - Success if exit code matches range\n- `\"Failure Exitcode Range\"` - Failure if exit code matches range\n- `\"Success Output Contains\"` - Success if output contains text\n- `\"Failure Output Contains\"` - Failure if output contains text\n**Default:** `\"Success Exitcode Range\"`\n**Usual Practice:** Use `\"Success Exitcode Range\"` for most extensions\n**Example:** `\"Success Exitcode Range\"`\n\n---\n\n### exitCodes\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** Conditional (Yes if exitCodeProcessing is \"Success/Failure Exitcode Range\")\n**Description:** Exit code(s) or range for success/failure determination\n**When to Use:** With exitcode-based processing\n**Format:**\n- Single code: `\"0\"`\n- Multiple codes: `\"0,1,5\"`\n- Range: `\"0-5\"`\n- Mixed: `\"0,5,10-20\"`\n**Usual Practice:** Use `\"0\"` for standard success code\n**Example:** `\"0\"`\n\n---\n\n### exitCodeText\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** Conditional (Yes if exitCodeProcessing is \"Success/Failure Output Contains\")\n**Description:** Text pattern to search for in output\n**When to Use:** With output-based processing\n**Note:** Supports regular expressions\n**Usual Practice:** Set to `null` unless using output-based exit code processing\n**Example:** `\"SUCCESS|COMPLETED\"` or `null`\n\n---\n\n### exitCodeOutput\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Path to file containing output to scan\n**When to Use:** When scanning specific output file instead of stdout/stderr\n**Usual Practice:** Set to `null` unless scanning specific output file\n**Example:** `\"/tmp/job_output.log\"` or `null`\n\n---\n\n### outputType\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Output source for exit code evaluation\n**When to Use:** With output-based exit code processing\n**Valid Values:**\n- `\"STDOUT\"` (default)\n- `\"STDERR\"`\n- `\"FILE\"`\n**Usual Practice:** Use `\"STDOUT\"` for standard output scanning\n**Example:** `\"STDOUT\"`\n\n---\n\n### exitCodeProcessingFieldsRestriction\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Visibility restriction for exit code processing fields\n**When to Use:** To control exit code field visibility in UI\n**Valid Values:**\n- `\"No Restriction\"` (default)\n- `\"Read Only\"`\n- `\"Hidden\"`\n**Usual Practice:** Use `\"No Restriction\"` to allow users to configure exit code handling\n**Example:** `\"No Restriction\"`\n\n---\n\n## Output Configuration\n\nProperties that control automatic output capture and retrieval.\n\n### outputReturnType\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Output capture strategy\n**When to Use:** To automatically retrieve and attach output to task instance\n**Valid Values:**\n- `\"NONE\"` - No output captured\n- `\"STDOUT\"` - Capture standard output\n- `\"STDERR\"` - Capture standard error\n- `\"FILE\"` - Capture from file\n- `\"OUTERR\"` - Capture both stdout and stderr (default)\n**Default:** `\"OUTERR\"`\n**Usual Practice:** Use `\"STDOUT\"` or `\"OUTERR\"` for most extensions to capture execution output\n**Example:** `\"STDOUT\"`\n\n---\n\n### outputReturnFile\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** Conditional (Yes if outputReturnType is \"FILE\")\n**Description:** Path to file containing output to retrieve\n**When to Use:** When capturing output from specific file\n**Usual Practice:** Set to `null` unless using FILE output type\n**Example:** `\"/var/log/backup_result.log\"` or `null`\n\n---\n\n### outputReturnSline\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** **YES when outputReturnType is \"STDOUT\"**\n**Description:** Starting line number for output retrieval\n**When to Use:** **REQUIRED** when outputReturnType is set to \"STDOUT\"\n**Default:** `\"1\"`\n**Usual Practice:** **Always set to \"1\" when using STDOUT output**\n**Example:** `\"1\"`\n\n---\n\n### outputReturnNline\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** **YES when outputReturnType is \"STDOUT\"**\n**Description:** Number of lines to retrieve from output\n**When to Use:** **REQUIRED** when outputReturnType is set to \"STDOUT\"\n**Default:** `\"100\"`\n**Usual Practice:** **Always set to \"100\" or desired line count when using STDOUT output**\n**Example:** `\"100\"`\n\n---\n\n### outputReturnText\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Text pattern to filter output (regex supported)\n**When to Use:** To extract specific lines from output\n**Note:** Controller processes as regular expression\n**Usual Practice:** Set to `null` unless filtering output\n**Example:** `\"ERROR.*|WARNING.*\"` or `null`\n\n---\n\n### outputFailureOnly\n\n**Type:** Boolean\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Only retrieve output on task failure\n**When to Use:** To reduce output storage for successful tasks\n**Default:** `false`\n**Usual Practice:** Set to `false` to capture output for all task executions\n**Example:** `false`\n\n---\n\n### outputContentType\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** MIME type for output content\n**When to Use:** For structured output (JSON, XML)\n**Usual Practice:** Omit unless parsing structured output\n**Example:** `\"application/json\"` or omit\n\n---\n\n### outputPathExpression\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** XPath expression for XML output parsing\n**When to Use:** When extracting specific data from XML output\n**Usual Practice:** Omit unless using XPath parsing\n**Example:** `\"/response/status/text()\"` or omit\n\n---\n\n### automaticOutputRetrievalFieldsRestriction\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Visibility restriction for output retrieval fields\n**When to Use:** To control output configuration field visibility in UI\n**Valid Values:**\n- `\"No Restriction\"` (default)\n- `\"Read Only\"`\n- `\"Hidden\"`\n**Usual Practice:** Use `\"No Restriction\"` to allow users to configure output settings\n**Example:** `\"No Restriction\"`\n\n---\n\n## Execution Behavior\n\nProperties that control how the extension executes.\n\n### alwaysCancelOnFinish\n\n**Type:** Boolean\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Execute cancel command when task is force-finished\n**When to Use:** When cleanup is required on force finish\n**Default:** `false`\n**Usual Practice:** Set to `true` if extension defines a cancel command for cleanup; otherwise `false`\n**Example:** `true`\n\n---\n\n### waitForOutput\n\n**Type:** Boolean\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Wait for output file generation before completing\n**When to Use:** When extension generates output file asynchronously\n**Default:** `false`\n**Usual Practice:** Set to `false` for most extensions unless async output generation is needed\n**Example:** `false`\n\n---\n\n### createConsole\n\n**Type:** Boolean\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Allocate new console for process (Windows only)\n**When to Use:** With `desktopInteract` for Windows GUI applications\n**Platform:** Windows only\n**Default:** `false`\n**Usual Practice:** Set to `false` for most extensions (rarely needed)\n**Example:** `false`\n\n---\n\n### desktopInteract\n\n**Type:** Boolean\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Allow desktop interaction for GUI applications\n**When to Use:** For applications requiring manual user interaction\n**Platform:** Windows XP/Server 2003 (limited support on newer Windows)\n**Default:** `false`\n**Usual Practice:** Set to `false` for automated extensions\n**Example:** `false`\n\n---\n\n### elevateUser\n\n**Type:** Boolean\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Execute with elevated privileges (bypass UAC)\n**When to Use:** For operations requiring administrator privileges\n**Platform:** Primarily Windows\n**Note:** Does not grant privileges not already available to account\n**Default:** `false`\n**Usual Practice:** Set to `false` unless extension requires elevated privileges\n**Example:** `false`\n\n---\n\n### autoCleanup\n\n**Type:** Boolean\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Automatically clean temporary files after execution\n**When to Use:** To prevent temporary file accumulation\n**Default:** `false`\n**Usual Practice:** Set to `false` for most extensions; UAC manages cleanup automatically\n**Example:** `false`\n\n---\n\n### autoDelete\n\n**Type:** Boolean\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Auto-delete extension archive after deployment\n**When to Use:** To save storage space (rarely used)\n**Default:** `false`\n**Usual Practice:** **Best practice is to omit this property entirely** or set to `null` as it's not commonly used\n**Example:** `null` or omit\n\n---\n\n### checkPreconditions\n\n**Type:** Boolean\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Check preconditions before execution\n**When to Use:** For validating execution requirements (rarely used)\n**Default:** `false`\n**Usual Practice:** **Best practice is to omit this property entirely** or set to `null` as it's not commonly used\n**Example:** `null` or omit\n\n---\n\n## Credential Configuration\n\nProperties for authentication and credentials.\n\n### credentials\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Credential name for agent execution\n**When to Use:** When tasks require specific credentials\n**Mutually Exclusive With:** `credentialsVar`\n**Note:** Overrides agent default credentials\n**Usual Practice:** Set to `null` unless requiring specific template-level credentials\n**Example:** `\"production-db-creds\"` or `null`\n\n---\n\n### credentialsVar\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Variable containing credential name at runtime\n**When to Use:** When credential name is dynamic\n**Mutually Exclusive With:** `credentials`\n**Format:** `\"${VARIABLE_NAME}\"`\n**Usual Practice:** Set to `null` unless using variable-based credentials\n**Example:** `\"${DB_CREDENTIALS}\"` or `null`\n\n---\n\n### credentialFieldsRestriction\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Visibility restriction for credential fields\n**When to Use:** To control credential field visibility in UI\n**Valid Values:**\n- `\"No Restriction\"` (default)\n- `\"Read Only\"`\n- `\"Hidden\"`\n**Usual Practice:** Use `\"No Restriction\"` to allow users to configure credentials\n**Example:** `\"No Restriction\"`\n\n---\n\n## Script Configuration\n\nProperties for script-based templates (less common for Extensions).\n\n### useCommonScript\n\n**Type:** Boolean\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Use same script for all platforms\n**When to Use:** For platform-agnostic scripts\n**Default:** `false`\n**Usual Practice:** Set to `false` for Universal Extensions (extensions don't typically use scripts)\n**Example:** `false`\n\n---\n\n### script\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** Conditional (Yes if useCommonScript is true)\n**Description:** Common script content for all platforms\n**When to Use:** With `useCommonScript: true`\n**Usual Practice:** Omit for Universal Extensions (not applicable)\n**Example:** `\"python3 /opt/scripts/backup.py\"`\n\n---\n\n### scriptUnix\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Linux/Unix-specific script\n**When to Use:** When agentType is \"Any\" or \"Linux/Unix\"\n**Usual Practice:** Omit for Universal Extensions (not applicable)\n**Example:** `\"#!/bin/bash\\n/opt/backup.sh\"`\n\n---\n\n### scriptWindows\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Windows-specific script\n**When to Use:** When agentType is \"Any\" or \"Windows\"\n**Usual Practice:** Omit for Universal Extensions (not applicable)\n**Example:** `\"powershell.exe -File C:\\\\Scripts\\\\backup.ps1\"`\n\n---\n\n### scriptTypeWindows\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Windows script file type\n**When to Use:** With Windows scripts\n**Valid Values:**\n- `\"bat\"` - Batch file\n- `\"cmd\"` - CMD script\n- `\"js\"` - JavaScript\n- `\"ps1\"` - PowerShell\n- `\"py\"` - Python\n- `\"uapy\"` - UA Python\n- `\"vbs\"` - VBScript\n- `\"wsf\"` - Windows Script File\n- `\"Other\"` - Other type\n**Usual Practice:** Omit for Universal Extensions (not applicable)\n**Example:** `\"ps1\"`\n\n---\n\n### runtimeDir\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Directory from which to execute\n**When to Use:** **NEVER for Universal Extensions** (always use `null`)\n**Note:** UAC manages runtime directories automatically for extensions\n**Default:** `null`\n**Usual Practice:** **Always set to `null` for extensions**\n**Example:** `null`\n\n---\n\n## Environment Variables\n\nProperties for environment variable configuration.\n\n### environment\n\n**Type:** Array\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Predefined environment variables for extension\n**When to Use:** To pass configuration via environment variables\n**Usual Practice:** Use empty array `[]` unless extension requires predefined environment variables\n**Structure:**\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ENV_VAR_NAME\",\n    \"value\": \"env_var_value\",\n  }\n]\n```\n**Example:**\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"API_ENDPOINT\",\n    \"value\": \"https://api.example.com\",\n  }\n]\n```\n\n---\n\n### environmentVariablesFieldsRestriction\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Visibility restriction for environment variable fields\n**When to Use:** To control environment variable field visibility in UI\n**Valid Values:**\n- `\"No Restriction\"` (default)\n- `\"Read Only\"`\n- `\"Hidden\"`\n**Usual Practice:** Use `\"No Restriction\"` to allow users to configure environment variables\n**Example:** `\"No Restriction\"`\n\n---\n\n### sendEnvironment\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** When to send environment variables\n**When to Use:** To control variable sending timing\n**Valid Values:**\n- `\"Launch\"` (default) - Send during task launch\n- `\"Dynamic Choice\"` - Send during dynamic choice command\n- `\"Dynamic Command\"` - Send during dynamic command\n**Format:** Comma-separated for multiple\n**Default:** `\"Launch\"`\n**Usual Practice:** Use `\"Launch,Dynamic Choice,Dynamic Command\"` for all standard extensions\n**Example:** `\"Launch,Dynamic Choice\"`\n\n---\n\n### sendVariables\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Variable scope to send to extension\n**When to Use:** To control which variables are passed\n**Valid Values:**\n- `\"None\"` - Don't send task variables\n- `\"Local\"` - Send local task variables\n**Default:** `\"None\"`\n**Usual Practice:** Use `\"None\"` unless extension needs access to task instance variables\n**Example:** `\"Local\"`\n\n---\n\n## Logging Configuration\n\nProperties for logging and debugging.\n\n### logLevel\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Extension logging verbosity\n**When to Use:** To control log detail level\n**Valid Values:**\n- `\"Inherited\"` (default) - Use agent/task log level\n- `\"Info\"` - Informational messages\n- `\"Debug\"` - Detailed debugging information\n- `\"Error\"` - Error messages only\n- `\"Fatal\"` - Fatal errors only\n**Default:** `\"Inherited\"`\n**Usual Practice:** Omit or use `\"Inherited\"` to follow system logging configuration\n**Example:** `\"Info\"`\n\n---\n\n## Field Restrictions\n\nProperties to control field group visibility.\n\nAll field restriction properties use the same values:\n- `\"No Restriction\"` - Fields visible and editable (default)\n- `\"Read Only\"` - Fields visible but not editable\n- `\"Hidden\"` - Fields not visible\n\n**Usual Practice:** Use `\"No Restriction\"` for all field restriction properties to provide full configurability to users\n\n### Available Restriction Properties\n\n- **agentFieldsRestriction** - Agent selection fields\n- **credentialFieldsRestriction** - Credential fields\n- **environmentVariablesFieldsRestriction** - Environment variable fields\n- **exitCodeProcessingFieldsRestriction** - Exit code processing fields\n- **automaticOutputRetrievalFieldsRestriction** - Output retrieval fields\n\n---\n\n## Runtime Components\n\nOptional arrays for dynamic behavior.\n\n### fields\n\n**Type:** Array\n**Required:** Yes (can be empty array)\n**Description:** UI field definitions\n**When to Use:** Always include (empty array if no fields)\n**Usual Practice:** Always include this array; populate with field definitions as needed\n**See:** **ue-template-standard-extension-fields.md** for field properties\n**Example:** `[]`\n\n---\n\n### commands\n\n**Type:** Array\n**Required:** Yes (can be empty array)\n**Description:** Extension command definitions for operations that can be invoked independently\n**When to Use:** For extension commands decorated with `@dynamic_command` in extension.py\n**Usual Practice:**\n- Use empty array `[]` if extension has no dynamic commands\n- Add one entry per `@dynamic_command` method in extension.py\n- Include only the fields (by fieldMapping name) that the command needs access to\n\n**Structure:**\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"asynchronous\": false,\n    \"executionOption\": \"Out Of Process\",\n    \"fields\": [\"Integer Field 1\", \"Credential Field 1\"],\n    \"label\": \"Validate Configuration\",\n    \"name\": \"validate_configuration\",\n    \"statuses\": [\"Defined\", \"Waiting\", \"Held\", \"Action Required\"],\n    \"timeout\": null\n  }\n]\n```\n\n**Properties:**\n- `asynchronous`: Boolean - whether command runs asynchronously (usually `false`)\n- `executionOption`: String - execution mode for the command\n  - **Available Values:**\n    - `\"Out Of Process\"` - Command runs in a separate process (recommended for most use cases)\n    - `\"In Process\"` - Command runs in the same process as the extension\n- `fields`: Array of fieldMapping names (e.g., `[\"Integer Field 1\", \"Credential Field 1\"]`) that the command needs access to\n- `label`: String - display name shown to users\n- `name`: String - must match the `command_name` in `@dynamic_command(command_name=\"...\")` decorator\n- `statuses`: Array of task statuses when command is available - specify which task statuses allow this command to be executed\n  \n  - **NEVER use an empty array `[]`** - UAC does not interpret empty arrays as \"any status\"\n  - If analysis states \"no status restriction\" or \"can execute at any time\", this means **list ALL valid statuses explicitly**\n  - Empty array `[]` = incomplete/missing field, NOT unrestricted access\n  - **Available Status Values:**\n    - `\"Defined\"` - Task is defined but not yet scheduled\n    - `\"Waiting\"` - Task is waiting to start\n    - `\"Time Wait\"` - Task is waiting for scheduled time\n    - `\"Instance Wait\"` - Task is waiting for another instance\n    - `\"Held\"` - Task is held manually\n    - `\"Exclusive Requested\"` - Exclusive resource requested\n    - `\"Exclusive Wait\"` - Waiting for exclusive resource\n    - `\"Resource Requested\"` - Resource has been requested\n    - `\"Resource Wait\"` - Waiting for resource availability\n    - `\"Execution Wait\"` - Waiting to execute\n    - `\"Undeliverable\"` - Task cannot be delivered\n    - `\"Queued\"` - Task is queued for execution\n    - `\"Submitted\"` - Task has been submitted\n    - `\"Action Required\"` - Task requires user action\n    - `\"Started\"` - Task has started\n    - `\"Running\"` - Task is currently running\n    - `\"Running/Problems\"` - Task is running with problems\n    - `\"Cancel Pending\"` - Cancel operation is pending\n    - `\"In Doubt\"` - Task status is uncertain\n    - `\"Start Failure\"` - Task failed to start\n    - `\"Confirmation Required\"` - Task requires confirmation\n    - `\"Cancelled\"` - Task was cancelled\n    - `\"Failed\"` - Task execution failed\n    - `\"Skipped\"` - Task was skipped\n    - `\"Finished\"` - Task has completed\n    - `\"Success\"` - Task completed successfully\n  - **Example Restricted:** `[\"Defined\", \"Waiting\", \"Held\", \"Action Required\"]` - Command available only in specific states\n  - **Example No Restriction:** `[\"Success\", \"Failed\", \"Finished\", \"Running\", \"Cancelled\", \"Waiting\", \"Held\", \"Skipped\", \"Action Required\", \"Defined\", \"Start Failure\", \"Running/Problems\", \"Cancel Pending\", \"In Doubt\", \"Confirmation Required\"]` - Command available at any time (all statuses)\n- `timeout`: Integer or null - command timeout in seconds (usually `null`)\n\n**Example Use Cases:**\n- Configuration validation commands\n- Connection test commands\n- Data refresh commands\n- System information retrieval\n\n---\n\n### events\n\n**Type:** Array\n**Required:** Yes (can be empty array)\n**Description:** Event definitions for external notifications\n**When to Use:** For integration with external event systems\n**Usual Practice:** Use empty array `[]` unless extension requires event notifications\n**Structure:**\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"event_name\",\n  }\n]\n```\n**Example:** `[]`\n\n---\n\n## Versioning & Import/Export\n\nProperties for version tracking and import/export behavior.\n\n### minReleaseLevel\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** Yes\n**Description:** Minimum UAC version required\n**When to Use:** Always required - must be specified for all Universal Extensions\n**Format:** Version string (e.g., \"7.2.0.0\")\n**Default:** `\"7.2.0.0\"`\n**Usual Practice:** Always set to `\"7.2.0.0\"` (standard minimum) or higher if using version-specific features\n**Example:** `\"7.2.0.0\"`\n\n---\n\n### exportReleaseLevel\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** UAC version when template was exported\n**When to Use:** Automatically populated on export\n**Note:** Read-only, set by system\n**Usual Practice:** Automatically populated by UAC during export; do not manually set\n**Example:** `\"7.4.1.0\"`\n\n---\n\n### retainSysIds\n\n**Type:** Boolean\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Retain sysIds during import\n**When to Use:** For updates to preserve field references\n**Note:** Recommended for updating Choice values\n**Default:** `true`\n**Usual Practice:** Set to `true` to preserve sysIds during updates\n**Example:** `true`\n\n---\n\n### excludeRelated\n\n**Type:** Boolean\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Exclude related records during export (rarely used)\n**When to Use:** For cleaner exports\n**Note:** Specified as attribute in XML\n**Default:** `false`\n**Usual Practice:** **Best practice is to omit this property entirely** or set to `null` as it's not commonly used\n**Example:** `null` or omit\n\n---\n\n## Icon Metadata (Optional)\n\nProperties for extension icon information.\n\n### iconDateCreated\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Icon creation timestamp\n**Usual Practice:** Automatically set by UAC when icon is uploaded; do not manually set\n**Example:** `\"2024-01-15T10:30:00Z\"`\n\n---\n\n### iconFilename\n\n**Type:** String\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Icon filename\n**Usual Practice:** Automatically set by UAC when icon is uploaded; do not manually set\n**Example:** `\"extension-icon.png\"`\n\n---\n\n### iconFilesize\n\n**Type:** Integer\n**Required:** No\n**Description:** Icon file size in bytes\n**Usual Practice:** Automatically set by UAC when icon is uploaded; do not manually set\n**Example:** `2048`\n\n---\n\n## Related Documentation\n\n- **ue-template-structure.md** - High-level template structure overview\n- **ue-template-standard-extension-fields.md** - UI field properties and metadata\n- **ue-template-architect-notes.md** - Best practices, examples, and design patterns\n- **universal-template-properties.mdx** - Complete UAC property specification\n",
      "numLines": 992,
      "startLine": 1,
      "totalLines": 992
    }
  },
